```bash
cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml --message-format=short 2>&1
```

### 3. Clear All Caches
```bash
rm -rf node_modules/.vite node_modules/.cache .next
pkill -f "tauri|vite" 2>/dev/null || true
```

### 4. Live Connection Monitoring
```typescript
// Add to cloud connector for debugging
setInterval(async () => {
  const stats = await this.getConnectionStats();
  console.log('Connection health:', stats);
}, 10000);
```

## Connection States

### Status Meanings
- **"Disconnected"**: No connection attempt
- **"Connecting"**: Initial connection in progress
- **"Reconnecting(N)"**: Failed N times, retrying
- **"Ready"**: Connected and authenticated
- **"Error"**: Permanent failure

### State Transitions
```
Disconnected → Connecting → Ready
     ↓              ↓         ↓
   Error ← Reconnecting(N) ←  Error
```

## Performance Monitoring

### Key Metrics
```typescript
interface ConnectionStats {
  connected_at?: number;
  total_commands: number;
  successful_commands: number;
  failed_commands: number;
  reconnection_count: number;
  last_heartbeat?: number;
  latency_ms?: number;
}
```

### Health Check Pattern
```typescript
async checkHealth(): Promise<boolean> {
  try {
    const stats = await this.getConnectionStats();
    return stats?.total_commands > 0 &&
           (stats.successful_commands / stats.total_commands) > 0.8;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Error Recovery Patterns

### 1. Automatic Reconnection
```rust
async fn handle_connection_error(&mut self, error: &CloudError) {
  self.reconnection_count += 1;
  if self.reconnection_count < MAX_RECONNECTION_ATTEMPTS {
    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(5)).await;
    self.establish_connection().await?;
  }
}
```

### 2. Circuit Breaker Pattern
```rust
if self.consecutive_failures > CIRCUIT_BREAKER_THRESHOLD {
  return Err(CloudError::CircuitBreakerOpen);
}
```

### 3. Graceful Degradation
```typescript
if (!await cloudConnector.isConnected()) {
  // Fall back to local-only mode
  console.warn('Cloud unavailable, using local agent only');
}
```

## Testing Checklist

Before deploying WebSocket changes:

- [ ] ✅ Compilation: `cargo check` passes
- [ ] ✅ Connection: Test script connects successfully
- [ ] ✅ Authentication: HMAC validation works
- [ ] ✅ Commands: Messages flow both directions
- [ ] ✅ Events: Frontend receives Rust events
- [ ] ✅ Errors: Graceful error handling
- [ ] ✅ Reconnection: Automatic recovery works
- [ ] ✅ Performance: No memory leaks or hangs

